  "worked_solution": "Isolating the cubic term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt[3]{6x-2}+8 & <10 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt[3]{6x-2} & <2 \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{6x-2} & <4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we cube both sides and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\sqrt[3]{6x-2})}^{3} & <{4}^{3} \\\\ 6x-2 & <64 \\\\ 6x & <66 \\\\ x & <11.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
